{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Pull Request Readiness Generator",
  "description": "Comprehensive PR preparation tool that analyzes code changes across frontend/backend/database, maps to spec tasks, runs quality checks, identifies risks, and generates detailed PR descriptions",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "userTriggered"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Generate a comprehensive Pull Request readiness report by:\n\n1. **Change Analysis**: \n   - Analyze git diff to summarize what changed in frontend (client/), backend (server/), and database (migrations, schema)\n   - Categorize changes: features, fixes, refactoring, dependencies, configuration\n   - Identify modified files and their purposes\n\n2. **Spec Task Mapping**:\n   - Review any spec files or task documentation to map completed changes to requirements\n   - Identify which spec tasks are now \"done\" based on the changes\n   - Note any incomplete or partially implemented features\n\n3. **Quality Assurance Commands**:\n   - List exact commands to run for linting, type checking, and testing\n   - For frontend: `cd secure-gate-access/client && npm run lint && npm test`\n   - For backend: `cd secure-gate-access/server && npm run lint && npm test && npm run test:integration`\n   - For E2E: `npm run test:e2e` (if applicable)\n   - Include any database migration or validation commands\n\n4. **Risk Assessment**:\n   - Identify high-risk areas based on changes (auth, database, security, external APIs)\n   - Propose specific verification steps for each risk area\n   - Suggest manual testing scenarios\n   - Note any breaking changes or migration requirements\n\n5. **PR Description Draft**:\n   Generate a complete PR description with:\n   - **What**: Clear summary of changes and features\n   - **Why**: Business justification and problem solved\n   - **How**: Technical approach and implementation details\n   - **Testing**: Manual and automated testing performed\n   - **Rollout Notes**: Deployment considerations, environment variables, migrations\n   - **Screenshots/Demo**: Placeholders for visual changes\n   - **Checklist**: Standard PR checklist items\n\n6. **Deployment Readiness**:\n   - Check for required environment variables or configuration changes\n   - Identify any database migrations that need to run\n   - Note any infrastructure or deployment script updates needed\n\nPlease provide actionable, specific guidance that a developer can follow to ensure their PR is complete and ready for review."
  }
}